# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
build/
dist/
.venv/

# Stub build intermediates (keep the .bin/.json blobs — they are package data)
sopack/stubs/*.elf
# The wbaes helper skeleton is USER-built per ABI against your own whitebox-cryptography
# and NDK (docs/wbaes-verification.md Phase 4), so it is a local artifact, not package data.
# sopack/stubs.py raises StubMissingError with build guidance when it is absent.
sopack/stubs/*.so

# Local keystores / scratch
*.keystore
*.apk
*.idsig
output/
.DS_Store
libvosWrapperEx-arm64.so

# Local binary/APK fixtures and third-party white-box artifacts — large, and not ours to
# redistribute. Tests that need them skip; tests/fixtures/ below is the committed substitute.
#
# FOUR separate things, deliberately four directories (see CLAUDE.md "Directory layout"). Only
# the first is tracked, and it is the only one that is a SOURCE:
#   third_party/whitebox-cryptography/
#               the pinned WBC dependency, a TRACKED git submodule. NOT ignored — it is the
#               source vendor/wbc/ is built FROM. Its own third_party/ (libsodium, O-MVLL) is
#               fetched by its fetch_deps.sh and ignored by its own .gitignore, not ours.
#   test_apks/  the local APK corpus scripts/device_test.sh runs. *.apk below already covers
#               what is in there today, but keep the directory rule so an unpacked APK tree
#               dropped in it does not turn `git status` into 1900 lines.
#   vendor/     third-party BUILD OUTPUTS of that submodule - vendor/wbc/ is the libwbcrypto.a +
#               wbcrypto.h + bin/wb_keygen that scripts/build_wbaes.sh builds and copies out.
#               Host- and ABI-specific, so it is generated per machine, never committed.
#   artifacts/  the GENERATED portable pack bundle from scripts/artifact_generation.sh. It is an
#               output, not a source: regenerate it, never edit it in place. (This was `assets/`
#               until the split - retired because assets/ is a real Android APK directory.)
test_apks/
vendor/
artifacts/
# ...and the tarball --tar writes NEXT TO the bundle (never inside it - an archive created in
# the directory it is archiving self-includes).
sopack-bundle-*.tar.gz

# ...except the small purpose-built test fixtures, which MUST be committed so the wbaes
# tests run on a bare clone (see tests/test_wbaes.py).
!tests/fixtures/
!tests/fixtures/**
